  ("Describe the parts of a classical Hindu temple. (5 marks)", "The temple has a ceremonial entrance (gopuram in the south, torana in some northern temples), one or more mandapas (pillared halls), and the garbhagriha, the innermost chamber with the image of the deity, facing east. Above it rises the shikhara (north) or vimana (south). Large complexes have prakaras (enclosures), secondary shrines and a pradakshina corridor. The temple is planned as the body of Purusha, and worship is a journey from the outer world to the inner shrine."),
